===================================================
    
Case 1: NUMERIC(38,-5) and NUMERIC(10,-2) columns convert to the same BIGINT as INTEGER     

===================================================
id    cast(n5 as bigint)    cast(n5 as integer)    cast(n2 as bigint)    cast(n2 as integer)    
1     1500000     1500000     1200     1200     

===================================================
    
Case 2: a negative value keeps its sign     

===================================================
id    cast(n5 as bigint)    cast(n2 as bigint)    
2     -1500000     -1200     

===================================================
    
Case 3: values next to the BIGINT maximum and minimum convert     

===================================================
cast( cast(9223372036854775800 as numeric(38,-2)) as bigint)    
9223372036854775800     

===================================================
cast( cast(-9223372036854775800 as numeric(38,-2)) as bigint)    
-9223372036854775800     

===================================================
    
Case 4: values past the BIGINT maximum and minimum fail with an overflow error     

===================================================
Error:-427
===================================================
Error:-427
===================================================
Error:-427
===================================================
Error:-427
===================================================
Error:-427
===================================================
    
Case 5: a scale of -18 converts, and a scale of -19 or less fails with an overflow error     

===================================================
cast( cast(9000000000000000000 as numeric(38,-18)) as bigint)    
9000000000000000000     

===================================================
Error:-427
===================================================
    
Case 6: zero converts to zero for any negative scale     

===================================================
cast(n20 as bigint)    cast( cast(0 as numeric(38,-30)) as bigint)    
0     0     

===================================================
    
Case 7: inserting a NUMERIC of a negative scale into a BIGINT column stores the value     

===================================================
0
===================================================
2
===================================================
id    b    
1     1500000     
2     -1500000     

===================================================
    
Case 8: adding a NUMERIC of a negative scale to a DATETIME adds the value as milliseconds     

===================================================
datetime '2000-01-01 00:00:00'+n5    
2000-01-01 00:25:00.0     

